      "content": "1. UNDERSTAND THE EXAMINER’S MINDSET (MOST IMPORTANT)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Understanding the examiner's mindset and applying a scientific approach is critical for spotting traps.",
        "Subject-Verb Agreement, Hidden Subjects, and Tense Consistency form the core baseline of error detection.",
        "Modifier errors require you to always identify and check the actual doer of the action.",
        "Parallelism, Comparison Errors, and Word Redundancy are high-difficulty, high-probability test areas."
      ],
